{%- comment -%}
  web-kit 0.1.0 · components/theme-toggle/theme-toggle.liquid

  One two-state button. The label never changes ("Dark theme"); aria-pressed says
  whether it is on. Which icon shows is decided only by CSS from [data-theme] and
  the OS preference — theme.js flips the attribute, never the icon, so the icon
  can't drift from the palette actually applied.

  Icons are the site's: replace wk-icon-light.liquid / wk-icon-dark.liquid. Each
  must be decorative (aria-hidden="true", focusable="false").
{%- endcomment -%}
<button type="button" class="wk-theme-toggle" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Dark theme">
  <span class="wk-theme-toggle__icon wk-theme-toggle__icon--light">{%- include "wk-icon-light.liquid" -%}</span>
  <span class="wk-theme-toggle__icon wk-theme-toggle__icon--dark">{%- include "wk-icon-dark.liquid" -%}</span>
</button>
